  "body": "### Summary\nDecide how #450 (legacy, built on #372: tab bar everywhere HFR-096, plus four UX corrections from Bybifok's feedback) relates to SwiftHFR, now that #372 is the legacy parity reference.\n\nMilestone: M4 (operator, 2026-11-08), **to decide and discuss**.\n\n### Context\n- Parity reference since 2026-11-08: `legacy/duo-inner-cover` @ `2fe43da3` (#372), see #655.\n- #450, head `legacy/ux-bybifok` @ `9bdd9f50`, is #372 plus 14 commits: the HFR-096 tab bar option on iPad and the open Duo (decided by the operator on 2026-11-03 for legacy), and four \"S\" corrections (one highlighted action in a topic, distinct symbols for new topic, reply and sidebar, a readable Favoris button). It is still open.\n\n### Options\n1. **#450 into legacy, and its parity into SwiftHFR:** merge #450, move the reference to its merge, and port its changes as named items (each with a GAP row and a spec).\n2. **Stay on #372, iterate SwiftHFR on its own:** #450 stays a legacy matter; SwiftHFR takes from it only what its own design decides, as optional (b) items.\n\n### Inputs for the decision\n- What each of the four corrections and HFR-096 would change in SwiftHFR today (SwiftHFR already has a tab bar in compact width and a sidebar in regular width: #540, LOT-186).\n- The standing rule not to port Bybifok's UX proposals unless the operator takes them on (bugs excepted).\n\n### Outcome\nThe decision written here and, if option 1, the reference update in AGENTS.md §2 and the items opened.\n",
